  "protocol": "The Sandbox",
  "name": "SAND Base OFT delegate-confused-deputy bridge drain",
  "summary": "OFTSand's approveAndCall let any holder make the token call an arbitrary target, checking only that the call's first argument was the caller. Calling LayerZero EndpointV2.setDelegate through it made the attacker the OFT's delegate; it then set its own receive config, forged inbound messages to mint unbacked SAND on Base and bridged it out to drain the Ethereum adapter.",
